# Shared packages (`@questorylabs/shared`, `@questorylabs/db`)

## Zod schemas

- Pattern: `export const XSchema = z.object({...})` + `export type X = z.infer<typeof XSchema>`.
- `packages/shared/src/index.ts` is already a 1500+ line barrel. Do not keep appending: new domains or large schema groups go in their own file (like `pagination.ts` / `safe-href.ts`) and are re-exported from the index.
- Any request/response contract consumed by both `apps/api` and `apps/web` belongs here — not in `apps/web/src/lib` (the enterprise types stranded in `apps/web/src/lib/enterprise-types.ts` are the anti-pattern).

## Server-only code

Session and OAuth crypto stay in the `@questorylabs/shared/session` and `@questorylabs/shared/oauth-state` subpath exports. Never re-export them (or any Node-only code) from the browser-safe barrel `src/index.ts`.

## Prisma (`packages/db`)

- Edit only `packages/db/prisma/schema.template.prisma`. The generated `schema.prisma` and Prisma client are build artifacts (`pnpm db:schema` / `db:generate`) — never edit or commit them, never fork per-app schemas.
- After schema changes, run `pnpm db:schema && pnpm db:generate` so `apps/api` picks up the regenerated client.

## Tests

Every exported helper/schema gets a colocated `*.spec.ts` (see `session.spec.ts`, `pagination.spec.ts`). Run with `pnpm --filter @questorylabs/shared test`.
